## Session annotation (2026-07-29, marked as commentary — not source)

Recorded because the thesis was empirically tested the same day it was filed:

- The vault model of AI is parametric knowledge — frozen at training time,
  decaying after. Every fatal in the day's sealed audition was a vault failure
  (a frontier model inventing a mission name it did not hold; API teachers
  "imagining" search receipts answered from memory).
- The conductor model is the operator's thesis operationalized: the conductor-qwen
  tune's measurable gain was not knowledge but *transmission discipline* —
  reach for evidence first, cite only what was actually retrieved, report junk
  hits honestly. A 27B trained this way matched Claude Sonnet 5 (17.50 vs 17.31
  /20, both zero fatals) on the conductor domain, blind-graded.
- The ruwāt's integrity obsession (purity in = purity out) is implemented in the
  v1.2 generation harness as mechanical grounding rules; a fabricated receipt is
  treated as a fabricated isnad — audit-fatal.
- PART TWO's "the architecture is the vessel" is the muezzin design stated in one
  line: no single seat is the conductor; the seat plan, verdict panel, witness
  stack, gates and hooks are jointly the conduit, and the operator holds liability
  for what it transmits. The rijal parallel is already literal in this substrate —
  `canon\model-rijal.md` keeps behavioural biographies of each model seat
  (dispatch constraints, known failure modes, verdict-accuracy records), which is
  'ilm al-rijal applied to machine transmitters.
- Live receipt of the same day: the frontier seat (Fable) exhausted its usage
  credits mid-run and three audit/mining agents died. The pipeline did not stop —
  the work re-routes to local open-weight seats on nxtbeast. A vessel whose
  integrity depends on one expensive node is a fragile vessel; the architecture
  degrading gracefully to local models IS the thesis under load.

Related book material: `canon\model-rijal.md`, `skills\hasan-li-ghayrihi\SKILL.md`
(the corroboration-upgrade grade — hasan li-ghayrihi: a weak chain strengthened by
independent corroboration), and the Isha/Kiraman-Katibin/assertion-ledger sessions
elsewhere in this folder.
